# The interceptor runs in the keystore domain (keystore on Android 10/11, keystore2
# on 12+) and binds an abstract unix socket; the root control daemon connects to it
# to push the resolved config. Grant the keystore side the socket-server permissions.
#
# The APatch launcher moves the daemon into system_server before app_process starts,
# so grant only that actual peer domain.  Do not reference the legacy Magisk root
# domain here: custom APatch treats such a rule as a minimal-v1 incompatibility and
# consequently cannot arm IReZygisk's domainless early loader.
allow keystore self unix_stream_socket { create bind listen accept getopt setopt read write shutdown }
allow system_server keystore unix_stream_socket connectto

# The `inject` binary attaches to the keystore process with PTRACE_ATTACH (it runs
# in the crash_dump domain), and keystore then dlopen()s the interceptor .so that
# lives under /data/adb (adb_data_file). Both are required for injection to work on
# an enforcing-SELinux device.
allow crash_dump keystore process *
allow keystore adb_data_file file *
